[F]Then [Bb]will Thy [C]servant [F]never fail
[F][Bb]To [C]deem [F]Thy [C]Sabbath [G7]doubly [C]blest,
[C][F]To [C7]deem [F][D7]Thy [Gm]Sabbath [Gm7][C7]doubly [F]blest.

{new_song}
{title: 394 - Far From All Care}
{artist: Seventh-day Adventist Hymnal}
{lyricist: }
{composer: }
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{tag: Doctrines}
{tag: }

Verse 1:
[F]Far [Bb]from [C7]all [F]care [F7]we [Bb]hail the [C]Sabbath [C7]morn[F]ing;
[F]O'er [A]waving [Dm]fields [Dm7]and [G]from the [G7]distant [C]sea
[F]Swell notes of [D]praise [D7]in [Gm]harmony re[F]sound[C]ing
[F]As all [F7]cre[Gm]ation [Bb]turns her [F]heart [C7]to [F]Thee.

Verse 2:
[F][Bb]Though [C7]man [F]alone, [F7]Lord, [Bb]of [C]Thy [C7]great [F]creation
[F]Fails [A]now [Dm]to laud [Dm7]Thee [G]for Thy [G7]love [C]and power,
[F]Yet [D]still [D7]a remnant [Gm]love [F]Thee [C]and remember
[F]Thy [F7]holy [Gm]law [Bb]and [F]each [C7]sweet [F]Sabbath hour.

Verse 3:
[F][Bb]Lord [C7]of [F]the [F7][Bb]Sabbath, [C]Savior [C7]and [F]Creator,
[F]Calm [A]now [Dm]the [Dm7]throbbings [G]of [G7]each [C]troubled breast.
